  "behavior": [
    "Admission captures a detached catalog/network and exact metadata definition or explicit absence. The private context is not published; review receives a detached network label and genesis hash.",
    "Current catalog/metadata is recaptured after asynchronous approval work and before signature release. Changes, including metadata appearing after absent admission, invalidate the request.",
    "Each local/external extrinsic uses a fresh TypeRegistry built from its captured definition, preventing cross-network registration leakage from the former global registry.",
    "Unsupported versions, disabled/ambiguous networks or metadata, unknown/duplicate signed extensions and custom-definition runtime-version mismatch reject at admission.",
    "Raw bytes have a disjoint payload shape and no chain identity; hybrids containing raw bytes and extrinsic discriminator fields reject.",
    "Extrinsic review uses the captured label/genesis instead of the live catalog; missing captured context blocks approval."
  ],
